# Categories

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Household
> Next Feature: Accounts

---

# Overview

Categories are labels for classifying transactions in Kin Finance.

Every transaction must belong to exactly one Category. Categories help users organize, filter, and budget their income and expenses.

In MVP, each Household has its own set of Categories. Categories are created and managed by the Owner. Members can view and use only categories that are visible to them.

---

# Goals

- Allow users to classify transactions into meaningful groups.
- Support budgeting by category.
- Give Owner control over which categories Members can see and use.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Create a Category.
- Edit a Category (name, type, visibility).
- Delete a Category.
- List all Categories visible to the current user.
- Toggle Category visibility for Members.

## Out of Scope

- Category icons (future).
- Category colors (future).
- Category grouping/nesting (future).
- Default category templates (future).

